.TH JOURNAL-SUMMARY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
journal-summary \- aggregate structured systemd journal priorities without messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B journal-summary
.RB [ --input " FILE|-]"
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads JSON Lines from a previously exported journalctl --output=json file
or from standard input. Counts PRIORITY 0 through 7. Missing or invalid
priority values are counted as UNKNOWN. Never prints original log contents,
identities, paths or messages. Does not execute journalctl.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read the specified ordinary file, or standard input (default). Symlinks
are rejected in file mode.
.TP
.B --null
Emit exactly three NUL-terminated fields per record; no TSV heading.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show usage and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Print the command name and version on standard output.
.SH OUTPUT
One row for each numeric priority in 0..7, one UNKNOWN row, and one TOTAL
row. Ordinary output uses PRIORITY, LEVEL and COUNT TSV columns.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All records parsed; all priorities valid (including empty input).
.TP
.B 1
Fully parsed but at least one priority missing or invalid.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.TP
.B 3
Unreadable, malformed, truncated or oversized input or missing JSON::PP.
.SH LIMITS
16 MiB total input; 128 KiB per line; 50,000 records. No partial output on
parse error or limit exceedance. Requires bounded finite input, not --follow.
Priority fields are client-controlled; results are not intrusion detection.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B journalctl --no-pager -n 100 --output=json | journal-summary
.br
.B journal-summary --input ./synthetic.jsonl --null
.SH NOTES
The tool is read-only. It does not access the native macOS Unified Log.
See the bilingual command guides for security and privacy limitations.
